        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "756d42fe-a80b-5be1-b83a-00f96cae672a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Luca Cordero di Montezemolo, Enzo Ferrari, Piero Ferrari, Jean Todt, Amedeo Felisa, Massimo Fumarola\n- Companies: Ferrari, Fiat S.p.A., Fiat Chrysler Automobiles NV, Confindustria, FIEG, Pininfarina\n- Products: Ferrari Ascari, Supercar Challenge, Bugatti Veyron, Aston Martin DBR9\n- Places: Turin, Netherlands, Nürburgring, Silverstone Circuit\n- Topics: automotive industry, corporate merger, competition judging, video game content\n\nFacts:\n- Luca Cordero di Montezemolo was born on 31 August 1947 and is an Italian businessman.\n- Luca Cordero di Montezemolo was formerly Chairman of Ferrari and formerly Chairman of Fiat S.p.A.\n- Luca Cordero di Montezemolo was also President of Confindustria and FIEG.\n- Fiat S.p.A., short for Fabbrica Italiana Automobili Torino, was an Italian holding company whose original and core activities were in the automotive industry.\n- On 29 January 2014, Fiat S.p.A. announced that it would merge into the new Netherlands-based holding company Fiat Chrysler Automobiles NV before the end of 2014.\n- Fiat S.p.A. was succeeded by Fiat Chrysler Automobiles NV.\n- In the Ferrari Ascari competition, the judges included Luca Cordero di Montezemolo, Piero Ferrari, Jean Todt, Amedeo Felisa, Massimo Fumarola, Pininfarina, and more than 22,000 users of the FerrariWorld website.\n- Piero Ferrari was identified as the second and only living son of Enzo Ferrari.\n- Supercar Challenge includes more than 40 cars, including Ferraris, the Bugatti Veyron, and the Aston Martin DBR9.\n- Supercar Challenge includes 22 tracks, including the Nürburgring Grand Prix section and the Silverstone Circuit.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
